window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-10cdc56de63926b8"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-cloud-setup\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security-cloud\">Codex Security Cloud 设置</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 Codex Security Cloud 扫描一个已连接的 GitHub 代码库，并审阅扫描发现项。之后，你可以开启对新提交的监控。</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud 在 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a> 中运行扫描。如果要在桌面应用或 CLI 中扫描本地代码库，请使用单独的 <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security 插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始之前</h2> <p>请使用具备 Codex Security Cloud 权限的工作区，并完成 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a> 设置。你需要有权限连接想要扫描的 GitHub 代码库。设置过程中可以创建其云端环境。</p> <p>如果无法使用该插件，请向工作区管理员确认访问权限。如果缺少某个代码库，请在代码库选择器中使用 <strong>Configure access（配置访问权限）</strong>，检查 GitHub 应用是否有权访问相应组织和代码库。如果你自己无法授予访问权限，请联系 GitHub 管理员添加该代码库。</p> <p><a id=\"1-install-and-open-the-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"1\">1. 安装并打开插件</h2> <ol> <li>在网页版 ChatGPT 或桌面应用中打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>。</li> <li>在插件市场中搜索 <strong>Codex Security Cloud</strong>。</li> <li>安装并启用插件，然后从已安装的插件列表或侧边栏打开 <strong>Security Cloud</strong>。</li> </ol> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/plugins/plugin_connector_1p_6317a32dbf5c81919acd66de6722daf5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开插件市场（需联网）</a></p> <p><a id=\"2-connect-github\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"2-github\">2. 连接 GitHub</h2> <p>确认工作区已设置 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a>。在插件中选择 <strong>Scan（扫描）</strong>。如果系统提示，请选择 <strong>Connect GitHub（连接 GitHub）</strong>，然后使用你自己的 GitHub 账户登录。每位发起扫描的人都需要单独连接，并且需要有权访问目标代码库。</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud 不支持工作区级别的 GitHub 连接。</p> <p><a id=\"3-start-a-repository-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"3\">3. 启动代码库扫描</h2> <ol> <li>在 <strong>New Scan（新建扫描）</strong>中选择代码库。</li> <li>查看环境设置。选择 <strong>Auto（自动）</strong>会在启动扫描时创建环境。选择 <strong>Customize（自定义）</strong>可使用已有环境。有关设置详情，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex cloud 环境</a>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Scan Method（扫描方式）</strong>下选择 <strong>One-Time Scan（单次扫描）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Create（创建）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中打开扫描并跟踪进度。等待扫描完成，再检查报告状态和目标，然后解读发现项。如果扫描失败或取消，请将当前输出视为未完成的审查。</p> <p><a id=\"4-review-findings-and-available-fixes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"4\">4. 审阅发现项和可用修复</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>。使用 <strong>Open findings（未关闭的发现项）</strong>查看状态为 <strong>New（新建）</strong>、<strong>Triaged（已分流）</strong>或 <strong>In Progress（处理中）</strong>的发现项。搜索列表，或使用 <strong>Filters（筛选器）</strong>缩小范围。<strong>Severity and status（严重性和状态）</strong>图表会汇总符合当前筛选条件的发现项。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security Cloud 的发现项列表筛选为新建、已分流和处理中，发现项表格上方显示严重性与状态图表</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 筛选并审阅未关闭的发现项。图中代码库、发现项和数量均为虚构数据。 </figcaption> <p>从扫描结果或 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>中打开一项发现。检查受影响的代码和修订版本、攻击者可能利用的路径以及验证证据。在决定问题是否适用之前，阅读所有尚未解决的假设。扫描没有报告发现项，并不能证明代码库中不存在漏洞。</p> <p>如果代码库发现项提供 <strong>Fix with Codex（使用 Codex 修复）</strong>，选择它会启动 Codex 对话，以便根据当前代码检查该发现项、实施修复并运行相关测试。请在那里审阅最终更改和测试证据。</p> <p>提交监控发现项也可能提供建议补丁。选择 <strong>Create draft pull request（创建拉取请求草稿）</strong>之前，请先审阅补丁。这些操作的影响不同，请按照对应发现项所示的工作流进行。</p> <p><a id=\"5-monitor-new-commits\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"5\">5. 监控新提交</h2> <p>审阅首次扫描后，你可以监控后续提交带来的更改：</p> <ol> <li>选择 <strong>Scan（扫描）</strong>，然后选择代码库并检查环境设置。</li> <li>在 <strong>Scan Method（扫描方式）</strong>下选择 <strong>Continuous Scanning（持续扫描）</strong>。Codex Security 会扫描代码库的默认分支。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Scan commit history from（扫描提交历史起点）</strong>。时间范围越长，所提供的上下文越多，但首次扫描也会耗时更久。</li> <li>可选：添加威胁模型范围说明。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Create（创建）</strong>。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: 新建扫描设置中显示虚构的 acme/web-app 代码库、持续扫描、main 分支和一周的提交历史</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 配置持续扫描。图中显示的代码库为虚构数据。 </figcaption> <p>若要调整监控，请打开 <strong>Repositories（代码库）</strong>，选择一个代码库，然后打开 <strong>Monitoring settings（监控设置）</strong>。你可以更改云端环境、选择要审查的历史天数，以及暂停或启用监控。选择 <strong>Save（保存）</strong>以应用更改。</p> <p>扫描所有者、获准编辑的人员和 Codex Security 管理员都可以更改监控设置。更改（包括暂停监控）会应用于工作区中该代码库的共享配置，而不仅是更改设置者本人。如果你没有编辑权限，请联系扫描所有者或 Codex Security 管理员。</p> <p>请在 <strong>Monitoring settings（监控设置）</strong>中审阅生成的威胁模型，并补充代码本身无法确定的部署或安全上下文。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">改进威胁模型</a>。</p> <p>有关构建、验证或结果解读的问题，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2d8d28cbaa954fc4\">云端常见问题</a>。若要审查 GitHub 拉取请求，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-862c857e0358aa15\">Security Review</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-cloud-setup\">Codex Security Cloud setup</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Run a first scan of a connected GitHub repository with Codex Security Cloud, then review its findings. Afterward, you can enable monitoring for new commits.</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud runs scans in <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a>. For scans of a local repository in the desktop app or CLI, use the separate <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security plugin</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Use a workspace with Codex Security Cloud access and <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a> set up. You need permission to connect the GitHub repository you want to scan. You can create its cloud environment during setup.</p> <p>If the plugin is unavailable, check access with your workspace administrator. If a repository is missing, use <strong>Configure access</strong> in the repository picker to check the GitHub app's organization and repository access. If you can't grant access yourself, ask your GitHub administrator to add the repository.</p> <h2 id=\"1-install-and-open-the-plugin\">1. Install and open the plugin</h2> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong> in ChatGPT on the web or in the desktop app.</li> <li>Search the plugin marketplace for <strong>Codex Security Cloud</strong>.</li> <li>Install and enable the plugin, then open <strong>Security Cloud</strong> from your installed plugins or sidebar.</li> </ol> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/plugins/plugin_connector_1p_6317a32dbf5c81919acd66de6722daf5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open plugin marketplace (online)</a></p> <h2 id=\"2-connect-github\">2. Connect GitHub</h2> <p>Confirm that <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a> is set up for your workspace. In the plugin, select <strong>Scan</strong>. If prompted, select <strong>Connect GitHub</strong> and sign in with your own GitHub account. Each person who starts scans needs their own connection and access to the repository.</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud doesn't support workspace connections.</p> <h2 id=\"3-start-a-repository-scan\">3. Start a repository scan</h2> <ol> <li>In <strong>New Scan</strong>, choose the repository.</li> <li>Review the environment. <strong>Auto</strong> creates an environment when you start. Use <strong>Customize</strong> to choose an existing environment. See <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex cloud environments</a> for setup details.</li> <li>Under <strong>Scan Method</strong>, select <strong>One-Time Scan</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Create</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Open the scan in <strong>Scans</strong> to follow progress. Wait for it to finish, then check the reported status and target before interpreting its findings. If it fails or is canceled, read the available output as an incomplete review.</p> <h2 id=\"4-review-findings-and-available-fixes\">4. Review findings and available fixes</h2> <p>Open <strong>Findings</strong>. Use <strong>Open findings</strong> to review findings with a <strong>New</strong>, <strong>Triaged</strong>, or <strong>In Progress</strong> status. Search the list or use <strong>Filters</strong> to narrow the results. The <strong>Severity and status</strong> chart summarizes the matching findings.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Codex Security Cloud findings filtered to New, Triaged, and In Progress, with a severity and status chart above the findings table</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Filter and review open findings. Repositories, findings, and counts are fictional. </figcaption> <p>Open a finding from the scan or from <strong>Findings</strong>. Check its affected code and revision, the path an attacker could take, and the validation evidence. Read any unresolved assumptions before deciding whether the issue applies. A scan with no reported findings doesn't establish that the repository has no vulnerabilities.</p> <p>When a repository finding offers <strong>Fix with Codex</strong>, selecting it starts a Codex conversation to check the finding against current code, implement a fix, and run relevant tests. Review the resulting changes and test evidence there.</p> <p>Findings from commit monitoring can instead offer a suggested patch. Review that patch before selecting <strong>Create draft pull request</strong>. These actions have different effects, so follow the workflow shown for the finding.</p> <h2 id=\"5-monitor-new-commits\">5. Monitor new commits</h2> <p>Once you've reviewed the first scan, you can monitor changes as new commits arrive:</p> <ol> <li>Select <strong>Scan</strong>, then choose the repository and review the environment.</li> <li>Under <strong>Scan Method</strong>, select <strong>Continuous Scanning</strong>. Codex Security scans the repository's default branch.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Scan commit history from</strong>. Longer windows provide more context, but the initial scan takes longer.</li> <li>Optionally add threat model scoping guidance.</li> <li>Select <strong>Create</strong>.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: New Scan settings with the fictional acme/web-app repository, continuous scanning, the main branch, and one week of commit history</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Configure continuous scanning. The repository shown is fictional. </figcaption> <p>To adjust monitoring, open <strong>Repositories</strong>, select the repository, and open <strong>Monitoring settings</strong>. You can change the Cloud environment, choose how many days of history to review, and pause or enable monitoring. Select <strong>Save</strong> to apply changes.</p> <p>The scan owner, people granted edit access, and Codex Security administrators can change monitoring settings. Changes, including pausing monitoring, apply to that repository's shared configuration in the workspace, not just to the person making the change. If you can't edit it, ask the scan owner or a Codex Security administrator.</p> <p>Review the generated threat model in <strong>Monitoring settings</strong> and update it with deployment or security context the code doesn't establish. See <a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">Improve the threat model</a>.</p> <p>For questions about builds, validation, or result interpretation, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-2d8d28cbaa954fc4\">Cloud FAQ</a>. To review GitHub pull requests, use <a href=\"#/article/a-862c857e0358aa15\">Security Review</a>.</p>"};
